# Planboard staging (planboard-dev.mlovera.dev) — configuration template.
#
# Copy to `.env.dev` ONLY if you need one. The staging service runs without it:
# everything it requires is in the compose `environment:` block.
#
#   cp example.dev.env .env.dev
#
# --- What must never go in here ------------------------------------------
# PB_DATABASE_URL. Staging is SQLite permanently, on its own volume, and that
# is the property that makes it safe to run unreleased code against. The
# compose file pins PB_DB=sqlite in `environment:` (which overrides this file),
# and in SQLite mode the app ignores PB_DATABASE_URL even when set — but do not
# lean on that. To test against realistic content, restore a dump into a
# scratch database.
#
# Mail is also deliberately absent. With no PB_MAIL_TRANSPORT the app falls back
# to a transport that sends nothing, so a staging build cannot mail real
# teachers. Naming a provider here without its key and sender throws at startup.

# Raise the login throttle (5 attempts / 15 min per IP) while poking at a build.
# PB_LOGIN_MAX_ATTEMPTS=1000
